\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro treads water, eyes  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  action. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Shin Kishima \par \uc2 575 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 September 2000\par 10:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Sept 25 (Reuters) - The euro was steady on Monday as the market remained nervous about a possible repeat of last week's concerted Group of Seven \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in support of the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The euro hovered near Friday's closing against the dollar but was a good two percent below peaks it had hit immediately after the surprise G7 \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the market remained unconvinced the euro had finally found a floor. \par \par \uc2  The market's reluctance to challenge central banks was reinforced after G7 policymakers said in a communique issued after their meeting on Saturday that the group would "continue to monitor developments closely and to cooperate in exchange markets as appropriate." \par \par \uc2  "I think investors have to want to buy the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and to buy it just because you think the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is around the corner is never enough to provide a durable recovery," said Steve Barrow, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Bear Stearns in London. \par \par \uc2  "At the same time, I also don't think the markets will aggressively test the downside this week." \par \par \uc2  The euro was trading slightly below $0.88 , little changed on the day but more than two cents below Friday's post-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  peaks. Against the Japanese yen, the euro was trading slightly lower at around 94.50 yen . \par \par \uc2  Financial markets were stunned by the concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy euros on Friday, particularly with the unexpected participation of the United States - which even after the action maintained that its "strong dollar" policy was unchanged. \par \par \uc2  It was the first such large-scale coordinated action since 1995, and traders had little doubt central banks would not easily let it be seen as a failure. \par \par \uc2  "It's obvious the G7 will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again - monetary authorities are particularly sensitive about their credibility so they're not likely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  just once and go away," said Ken Landon, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Deutsche Bank. \par \par \uc2  CAPITAL FLOWS, DANISH REFERENDUM WEIGH ON EURO \par \par \uc2  Yet the pullback from the post-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  peaks on Friday was seen as a proof of the underlying pressure on the euro, whose losses against the dollar since its launch in 1999 reached 28 percent when it hit record lows below $0.8440 last week. \par \par \uc2  Investment in U.S. businesses and securities continued to attract European capital, while concerns lingered over the euro-zone inflation rate, which was running above the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target. \par \par \uc2  In addition, a Danish referendum on Thursday on the country's euro entry was seen providing a further blow to investors' confidence in the euro, with the "No" voters increasing their lead in opinion polls over the last few weeks. \par \par \uc2  The latest poll released on Monday showed opponents of Denmark joining the euro leading supporters by eight points. \par \par \uc2  Furthermore, dealers scented a whiff of differences within the G7 as the U.S. commitment to a strong dollar was seemingly at odds with a euro-supportive policy. \par \par \uc2  Treasury Secretary Larry Summers reaffirmed his commitment to a "strong dollar" policy after Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "We want to see how serious the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  is in lending support to the euro, while the country's strong dollar policy stays in place," said Masayuki Yamamoto, assistant vice president at Bank of America in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was little changed on the day against the yen, holding within a half yen of Friday's one-month highs around 108.15 yen . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw9p06o2l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
