\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Markets start cautiously, eye G7 on euro. \b0\par\par\uc2 468 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 September 2000\par 22:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SYDNEY, Sept 25 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets began the week cautiously on Monday after concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  supporting the euro on Friday was followed by a stern warning by the G7 during the weekend. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  caught the market off-guard, not only because it came before the Prague G7 meeting on Saturday, but also because it included Federal Reserve participation. \par \par \uc2  At 7:40 a.m. (2040 GMT) the euro was trading at US$0.8798/8803, slightly firmer than its US$0.8766 level in late New York trading on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The euro, which was on the verge of collapse last week when it struck yet another all-time low of 84.39 cents, had rallied briefly to just above 90.15 cents on Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  before falling back. \par \par \uc2  "The fact that we have had just about every \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in illustrates to me how serious they are about changing sentiment and changing the direction," said Mark Adams, head of institutional sales at National Australia Bank. \par \par \uc2  "My feeling is that it probably will put a base in because the market will start to look at a level like 85 cents as being a floor for the time being, provided they come back anD reinforce it if we trade down to those levels," he said. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen the euro was 94.90/95.00 compared with 94.98 on Friday, up from last week's low of 90.05. \par \par \uc2  G7 TALK, ACT TOUGH \par \par \uc2  All G7 central banks \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in support of the euro, in the first concerted move since 1995. It was also the first time the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  since its birth 20 months ago. \par \par \uc2  The G7 includes Britain, Canada, France, Germany, Italy, Japan and the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  U.S. participation in the round of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was the biggest shock for markets, which had expected the Federal Reserve to stay on the sidelines until after U.S. Presidential elections in November. \par \par \uc2  The G7 communique released on Saturday was also more stern than expected, warning that rich nations were ready to defend the world economy from high oil prices and the weak euro. \par \par \uc2  "In light of recent developments we will continue to monitor (the market) closely and to cooperate in exchange markets as appropriate," the communique said. \par \par \uc2  One hurdle facing the euro will be this Thursday's referendum in Denmark on whether to join the European Union's single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , although a "No" vote has largely been priced in. \par \par \uc2  Denmark's latest Megafon research institute's survey found 51 percent of respondents were opposed to euro membership, compared with 40 percent in favour. The rest were undecided. \par \par \uc2  Megafon's previous poll released on September 15 gave euro opponents a nine-point lead, 49-40 percent. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw9o06n1y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
