\par\par \b \uc2  Euro starts trading up vs USD in Asia - NZ dealers. \b0\par\par\uc2 253 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 September 2000\par 20:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WELLINGTON, New Zealand (Reuters) - The euro was higher against the U.S. dollar in Asian trade Monday after the Group of Seven (G7) nations signalled over the weekend that further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the behalf of the euro could not be ruled out. \par \par \uc2  After the market opened, the euro first traded at $0.8770 against the dollar from its New York Friday close of $0.8766 but down against the yen at 94.50, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers in New Zealand-based banks said. \par \par \uc2  The euro/yen closed in New York on Friday at 94.98. \par \par \uc2  "I think the market is going to be looking for further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but I think the euro will struggle to make gains above $0.8850 through this session," one \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "The market will be using any opportunity that we see the central banks in this time zone \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a chance to sell." \par \par \uc2  On Friday, all G7 central banks \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in concert to boost the sagging euro on foreign exchanges - the first coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since 1995, stunning markets who had been betting the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not agree to sell dollars ahead of presidential elections in November. \par \par \uc2  It was also the first time the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  since its birth 20 months ago. \par \par \uc2  The G7 finance ministers and central bankers meeting on Saturday reinforced the move, issuing a communique that stressed concern over the euro and made plain they were ready to do it again. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw9o06mzy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
