\par\par \b \uc2  Euro rallies, traders cite further  \highlight22\uc2 fx intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 198 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 September 2000\par 14:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Sept 22 (Reuters) - The euro rallied more than half a cent against the dollar and 2-1/2 yen against the yen as traders said central banks were once more buying euros against a range of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said earlier on Friday that the monetary authorities of the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Japan joined it in concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  because of their shared concern about the potential implications of recent movements in the euro exchange rate for the world economy. \par \par \uc2  The UK Treasury also said the UK authorities joined the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Traders said the authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday for a second time after the euro retreated from initial post-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  highs. \par \par \uc2  "We are seeing everyone, just about everywhere," said a trader from a Japanese bank in London. "We are seeing it in euro/dollar, euro/Canadian dollar." \par \par \uc2  The euro rose more than half a cent against the dollar in the space of a few minutes, rallying above $0.89 but failing to mount highs above $0.90 hit earlier, according to Reuters data. \par \par \uc2  It also rose to around 96 yen, but stopped short of earlier highs above 96.50 . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw9m06zjo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
