\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro blasted higher by joint  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Swaha Pattanaik \par \uc2 384 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 September 2000\par 14:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Sept 22 (Reuters) - The euro shot higher on Friday as major industrial powers unleashed joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's support a day before the meeting of the Group of Seven nations. \par \par \uc2  The official euro-buying spree was spearheaded by the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the first time the young \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on its own account, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Japan and Britain all joining in action which boosted the euro more than five percent on the day against the dollar and the yen. Dealers have not seen the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2 , European, and Japanese authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in concert since 1995 and the shock of seeing the United States weigh in meant the impact of the action was all the greater. \par \par \uc2  "The real surprise is that we have the Fed in," said Jeremy Hawkins, chief economic adviser at Bank of America in London. \par \par \uc2  "It has caught a lot of people by surprise and to that extent it is a major shock to the system and has that much more of a market impact." \par \par \uc2  The ECB said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been launched because of concern about the potential implications of recent moves in the euro, which had lost as much as 28 percent of its value against the dollar since its January 1999 launch. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. and Japanese authorities said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been launched at the ECB's initiative and that they participated because of their shared concern about the potential implications of recent movements in the euro for the world economy. \par \par \uc2  The ECB has repeatedly warned that the euro's protracted slide posed inflation risks to the 11-nation euro zone and said in its monthly bulletin released on Thursday the euro's exchange rate was increasingly out of line with economic reality. \par \par \uc2  The International Monetary Fund, whose annual meeting is currently underway in Prague, had said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  should not be a "taboo" earlier this week, though it had attracted criticisms for its comments from euro zone policymakers. \par \par \uc2  The euro rose above $0.90 for the first time since September 4 as a result of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , hitting peaks above 96.50 yen according to Reuters data. That compares with record lows below $0.8440 it had set earlier this week. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw9m06ze5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
