\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro edges up, helped by Intel, pre-G7 wariness. \b0\par\par\uc2 773 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 September 2000\par 05:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sept 22 (Reuters) - Falling U.S. stock futures, hit by a profit warning from chipmaker Intel Corp, rescued the euro from record-low territory in Tokyo on Friday, while traders were wary of aggressive moves ahead of a weekend Group of Seven meeting. \par \par \uc2  Worries over the euro lingered, however, as the market cautiously awaited word from Saturday's gathering of G7 finance ministers on what - if anything - the industrialised nations would do about the struggling European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "An overnight fall in crude oil prices and the Intel news helped spur euro short-covering ahead of the meeting. With the market quite short of euros, this was a good chance to unwind those positions ahead of the key event," a city bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "The market has to watch what happens at the G7, since it is likely to set the long-term trend for the euro," he said. \par \par \uc2  At 0230 GMT, the euro was quoted at 91.81/96 yen after briefly hitting a one-week high of 92.13 yen . It had traded around 91.40/50 yen in late U.S. dealings on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Against the dollar, the euro also firmed to $0.8595/8600 against Thursday's U.S. level of $0.8583/88. \par \par \uc2  News that Intel Corp's third quarter revenue will fall below forecast hammered the company's shares and spilled over into the rest of the market, driving the Nasdaq and S&P 500 futures contracts sharply lower during Asian trade. \par \par \uc2  "The Intel news clearly dealt a blow to the dollar, especially against the euro," a trust bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "Some speculation also emerged that the United States may be worried about the falling euro and would become more interested in bolstering the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  if it decided the euro's weakness would hurt overall U.S. corporate earnings in the long term." \par \par \uc2  As of 0245 GMT, the December Nasdaq futures contract was down its 92-point limit at 3,673.00, while December S&P 500 futures dropped 26.20 points to 1,443.30. \par \par \uc2  Despite speculation about U.S. concern over the euro, comments by U.S. Treasury Deputy Secretary Stuart Eizenstat overnight indicate the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not keen on joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Eizenstat said the U.S. administration's policy on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained unchanged. Treasury officials have frequently said they favoured a strong dollar because it helps keep inflation down. \par \par \uc2  But the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in a monthly report released on Thursday, voiced growing irritation with the euro's weakness and said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was getting increasingly out of step with economic reality and posed a major risk to stability. \par \par \uc2  Market speculation is intensifying over whether the ECB would conduct \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on its own, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "There are some doubts about the likely effectiveness of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if it is not done jointly with the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Japan, but I don't feel that way," another Japanese city bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "Of course there are real money flows into the United States from Europe which are pressuring the euro, but speculative forces are also substantial," he said. "Speculators are still betting the ECB won't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , so any actual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  should have a sizeable effect in pushing up the euro." \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the dollar was quoted at 106.84/87 yen , down from its earlier high of 107.06 but up from the late U.S. level of 106.54 yen on Thursday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Japanese exporters and institutional investors were rumoured to be placing heavy offers between 107.20 and 107.40 yen. They were also placing euro offers above 92 yen, dealers said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0316 GMT. All data taken from Reuters \par \par \uc2  with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130 \par \par \uc2  GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab      Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   1999 Cls\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab   21 Sep.\par \tab \tab \tab      -----------------------------------------\par  Euro/dlr\tab \tab   0.8595   0.8614   -0.22   -14.65   1.0070\par  Dlr/yen\tab \tab    106.84   106.54   +0.28    +4.53   102.21\par  Euro/yen\tab \tab    91.82    91.40   +0.46   -10.94   103.10\par  Dlr/swiss\tab \tab  1.7626   1.7610   +0.09   +10.84   1.5902\par  Stg/dlr\tab \tab    1.4369   1.4378   -0.06   -11.17   1.6176\par  Can/dlr\tab \tab    1.4872   1.4867   +0.03    +2.88   1.4455\par  Aus/dlr\tab \tab    0.5458   0.5450   +0.15   -16.84   0.6563\par  Euro/swiss\tab \tab 1.5148   1.5150   -0.01    -5.54   1.6036\par  Euro/stg\tab \tab   0.5982   0.5984   -0.03    -4.12   0.6239.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw9m06yz4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
