\par\par \b \uc2  ECB flexes muscles - with little help of its friends. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Tomasz Janowski \par \uc2 783 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 September 2000\par 18:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  FRANKFURT, Sept 22 (Reuters) - The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , long accused of paying lip service to the beleaguered euro, showed on Friday it was ready to take on markets, even if it had to enlist help from powerful friends to drive the message home. \par \par \uc2  The ECB, aided by the U.S. and Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , stepped into \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets buying euros, driving the central \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  up sharply to well above recent record lows. \par \par \uc2  Its first full-scale \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the euro since the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's launch in January 1999 marks its coming of age and will lend badly needed authority to the young institution. \par \par \uc2  It should also improve its standing with the sceptical public in the 11-member euro zone, particularly in Germany which replaced its once mighty D-mark with the ever sliding euro. \par \par \uc2  But analysts said the bank clearly felt it needed backing from the powerful and respected U.S. Federal Reserve to minimize the risk of the \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  backfiring. \par \par \uc2  "Had it gone and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  without the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it would have run a grave risk and that is why it didn't do it before, so the key player was the United States," Alison Cottrell, senior European economist at Paine Webber, said. \par \par \uc2  Friday's round of euro buying had already raised the stakes for those betting against the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and made it potentially more costly to keep driving it lower. \par \par \uc2  The move proved right those who considered sales of 2.5 billion euros of the ECB's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves announced last week as a dry run for a full-blown \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and will make markets more alert to similar signals in the future. \par \par \uc2  JURY STILL OUT \par \par \uc2  But it remains to be seen whether the action will have a lasting impact. Only by stemming the euro's long slide can the ECB seriously boost its stature and credibility in the market. \par \par \uc2  "Credibility of the ECB now depends on the success of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Elga Bartsch of Morgan Stanley Dean Witter in London. \par \par \uc2  Economists said the fact that the Bank of Japan and the Fed also put their reputation on the line bodes well for the success of the \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "This \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is highly significant and will put a floor under the euro. It's the fact that the Fed has joined that is important," said Glenn Davies at Credit Lyonnais in London. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders, who had for weeks tested the ECB's resolve to put its money where its mouth was by buying what it said was an undervalued \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , grew increasingly wary of a possible rebound in the euro ahead of the summit of the Group of Seven industrial nations this weekend. \par \par \uc2  This provided the ECB with a perfect opportunity to swing into action, while the support of the U.S. Federal Reserve caught markets off-guard. \par \par \uc2  DANES, OIL, PROFIT-WARNINGS \par \par \uc2  Economists said a range of factors pushed the central banks into action, including market nervousness after recent euro lows and next week's Danish vote on eurozone membership. \par \par \uc2  Some analysts said a spate of profit warnings by U.S. companies, whose exports hit by the weak euro, could have tipped the balance in favour of U.S. participation despite looming presidential elections. \par \par \uc2  Even if some market watchers remain sceptical whether Friday's action will reverse the 20-month downward trend in the euro, it certainly put the ECB at the centre of attention. \par \par \uc2  For months, its assertions that the euro's dollar rate was out of step with economic fundamentals and posed threats of inflation fell on deaf ears, eventually leading to fresh bouts of euro selling. \par \par \uc2  But with the baptism of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  behind it, markets may now pay more attention to what the ECB says about the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  WARNINGS IGNORED \par \par \uc2  With hindsight, the bank's September monthly report published on Thursday could have set off alarm bells in trading rooms, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  In its strongest language to date, the ECB expressed its mounting irritation with the euro rate. \par \par \uc2  "Standard economic reasoning seems increasingly insufficient to provide a convincing justification for the external value of the euro," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said. \par \par \uc2  Some analysts said the focus on verbal signals concerning the single European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  now shifts to across the Atlantic. \par \par \uc2  "Everybody knows what is the ECB's position on the euro, now the markets will have to be more attentive to the language the U.S. uses," Cottrell said. \par \par \uc2  "U.S. policymakers will have to do a balancing act saying they don't want an excessively weak euro but at the same time avoiding saying that they favour a weak dollar," she said. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw9m06fe5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
