\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro hangs in balance, looks to G7. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Carolyn Cohn \par \uc2 595 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 September 2000\par 09:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Sept 21 (Reuters) - The euro recovered from the previous day's record lows against the yen and the dollar on Thursday, looking to support from the Group of Seven finance ministers meeting this weekend to save it from new lows. \par \par \uc2  Ongoing negative sentiment towards the euro and the economies of the euro zone was balanced only by wariness of what the G7 might come up with, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "G7 ministers have a chance of trying to do something for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  - there has been plenty of verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and markets are tired of this talk," said Fabio Fraschetti, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Banca Nazionale del Lavoro in London. \par \par \uc2  G7 finance ministers meet in Prague on Saturday. \par \par \uc2  The euro traded near 90 yen on Thursday, according to Reuters data, before recovering to 90.86/91 by 0730 GMT. \par \par \uc2  It weakened to $0.8462 on Thursday, according to Reuters data, within a quarter cent of Wednesday's record lows, before rising above $0.85. \par \par \uc2  Japanese financial daily Nihon Keizai Shimbun reported on Thursday that the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) may have started considering solo \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the euro's slump. \par \par \uc2  The report quoted ECB sources as saying it was unrealistic to persist with the option of tripartite \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Japan and Europe. \par \par \uc2  But the report also said it was unclear whether the ECB would conduct unilateral \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy euros as there were concerns within the ECB that such action would have only a limited effect. \par \par \uc2  The market shrugged off the report as the sourcing was vague. \par \par \uc2  SUMMERS WATCHING OIL \par \par \uc2  U.S. Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers underlined Washington's reluctance to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  late on Wednesday by reiterating support for the U.S. "strong dollar" policy. \par \par \uc2  But Summers also said he was "closely watching" world \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and energy markets, leaving the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  open, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The euro found it hard to pull far from the previous day's record lows after Wednesday's news that the Ifo Institute's West German business climate index fell for the third month in a row, and of slower-than-expected gross domestic product growth in Italy, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "The euro was already desperately weak, and under this disappointing situation, weak economic data has almost confirmed market doubts about the euro-zone economy," said Ryohei Muramatsu, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Commerzbank in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  News of slower-than-expected economic activity in Japan in July briefly propped up the dollar against the yen JPY=) in early trade. But the dollar soon retreated to near 106.50 yen, where large stop-loss sales are said to be lurking. \par \par \uc2  Economic activity in Japan slowed 1.0 percent in July from the previous month, the Ministry of International Trade and Industry's (MITI) all-industries index showed on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  A core component of the all-industries index, the tertiary sector, mainly comprising service industries, fell 1.1 percent. \par \par \uc2  These indices are seen as useful pointers to gross domestic product data, suggesting that the third quarter got off to a soft start, though analysts remain reasonably confident of a bounce back in August and September. \par \par \uc2  At 0730 GMT, the dollar stood at 106.62/63 yen, a little above the previous day's one-week lows. \par \par \uc2  The New Zealand dollar dropped to new record lows of $0.4010, according to Reuters data, in tandem with weakness in the euro and the Australian dollar. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was a short-term risk of the sickly kiwi falling below US$0.40. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw9l06zlw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
