\par\par \b \uc2  Euro off lows as sellers hang fire ahead of G7. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Chikafumi Hodo \par \uc2 1,200 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 September 2000\par 08:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      TOKYO, Sept 21 (Reuters) - The euro drifted near lifetime \par \par \uc2  lows in late Tokyo on Thursday, treading water on the slim chance \par \par \uc2  it would be thrown a lifeline by Saturday's meeting of Group of \par \par \uc2  Seven finance ministers. \par \par \uc2      Follow-up sales were limited as short holders were hesitant \par \par \uc2  to boost already huge positions before the G7 meeting. \par \par \uc2      Sentiment for the euro stayed bearish with another set of \par \par \uc2  disappointing euro-zone economic data released on Wednesday \par \par \uc2  depressing the mood further, dealers said. \par \par \uc2      The slumping \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  changed hands through brokers at a low \par \par \uc2  of 90.11 yen on Thursday, just shy of its 90.05 yen lifetime low \par \par \uc2  set in overseas markets on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2      At 0540 GMT, the euro stood at 90.24/38 yen compared to \par \par \uc2  Wednesday's U.S. level of 90.58 yen. \par \par \uc2      It stood at $0.8480/90 still near its lifetime low of $0.8439 \par \par \uc2  set on EBS on Wednesday, traders said. \par \par \uc2      Early rounds of sales by Japanese exporters pushed the euro \par \par \uc2  to the intraday low, but activity thinned in the afternoon. \par \par \uc2      Options-linked bids aimed at protecting the euro at 90.00 yen \par \par \uc2  also limited aggressive sales, although many operators were \par \par \uc2  looking for chances to sell on rallies, they said. \par \par \uc2      "The market is sitting on its hands until it confirms the \par \par \uc2  outcome of the G7 meeting," a senior U.S. bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2      "People want to see whether the G7 nations will specifically \par \par \uc2  mention the euro in their communique. Without that, things could \par \par \uc2  turn more ugly for the euro," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2      Japanese financial daily Nihon Keizai Shimbun reported on \par \par \uc2  Thursday that the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) may have started \par \par \uc2  considering solo \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the euro's slump. \par \par \uc2      The report quoted ECB sources as saying it was unrealistic to \par \par \uc2  persist with the option of tripartite \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Japan and Europe. \par \par \uc2      But the report also said it was unclear whether the ECB would \par \par \uc2  conduct unilateral \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy euros as there are \par \par \uc2  concerns within the ECB that such action would have only a \par \par \uc2  limited effect. \par \par \uc2  The market shrugged off the report as the sourcing was vague. \par \par \uc2  The euro stayed under pressure in Tokyo in reaction to \par \par \uc2  Wednesday's news that the Ifo Institute's West German business \par \par \uc2  climate index fell for the third month in a row, and of \par \par \uc2  slower-than-expected gross domestic product growth in Italy. \par \par \uc2  "The euro was already desperately weak, and under this \par \par \uc2  disappointing situation, weak economic data has almost confirmed \par \par \uc2  market doubts about the euro-zone economy," said Ryohei \par \par \uc2  Muramatsu, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Commerzbank in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  News of slower-than-expected economic activity in Japan in \par \par \uc2  July briefly propped up the dollar against the yen in early \par \par \uc2  trade. But the dollar soon retreated to near 106.50 yen, where \par \par \uc2  large stop-loss sales are said to be lurking. \par \par \uc2  Economic activity in Japan slowed 1.0 percent in July from \par \par \uc2  the previous month, the Ministry of International Trade and \par \par \uc2  Industry's (MITI) all-industries index showed on Thursday. \par \par \uc2      A core component of the all-industries index, the tertiary \par \par \uc2  sector, mainly comprising service industries, fell 1.1 percent. \par \par \uc2      These indices are seen as useful pointers to gross domestic \par \par \uc2  product data, suggesting that the third-quarter got off to a soft \par \par \uc2  start, though analysts remain reasonably confident of a bounce \par \par \uc2  back in August and September. \par \par \uc2      At 0547 GMT, the dollar stood at 106.58/63 yen against \par \par \uc2  106.50/60 in U.S. trade late on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2      Elsewhere, the Australian dollar was adrift below 54 U.S. \par \par \uc2  cents on Thursday, after dipping to another all-time low of 53.63 \par \par \uc2  cents overnight, with the G7 meeting the only potential life raft \par \par \uc2  in sight. \par \par \uc2      The New Zealand dollar dropped to new low of $0.4010, \par \par \uc2  pressured by selling from a local bank. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said there was short-term risk of the sickly kiwi \par \par \uc2  falling below 40 cents. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0602 GMT. All data taken from Reuters \par \par \uc2  with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130 \par \par \uc2  GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab      Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   1999 Cls\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab   #N/A Bad TSDS.\par \tab \tab \tab      -----------------------------------------\par  Euro/yen\tab \tab    90.50    90.17   +0.37   -12.22   103.10\par  Dlr/swiss\tab \tab  1.7794   1.7760   +0.19   +11.90   1.5902\par  Stg/dlr\tab \tab    1.4130   1.4108   +