\par\par \b \uc2  IMM  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  mixed early, euros under pressure. \b0\par\par\uc2 501 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 September 2000\par 16:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  CHICAGO, Sept 20 (Reuters) - Euro futures retreated on Wednesday after an early attempt to claw back toward steady, remaining in negative territory and under pressure from negative sentiment that again took December to a new contract low overnight. \par \par \uc2  The December euro fell to $0.84780 on Globex, below the previous $0.85150 all-time low set on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers and locals participated in quiet dealings as the nearby euro trimmed losses early, one Chicago Mercantile Exchange floor broker said. However, the contract soon slipped toward pit session lows. \par \par \uc2  Japan's Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Haruhiko Kuroda said soon after the pit open that it would be troublesome if the euro did not recover soon. Kuroda will be attending the Group of Seven meeting of finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors in Prague on Saturday. \par \par \uc2  "Part of the problem out of Japan in general is the jawboning is so frequent that nobody reads a whole lot into it," said David Solin, partner at \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Analytics. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the euro could push into positive territory ahead of the G7 meeting of industrialised nations. Short covering could lift euro futures, with the market uncertain about the meeting's outcome. \par \par \uc2  "The closer you get to the weekend, the more caution will come in, even though it's going to take G3 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to really turn this thing around," the broker said. \par \par \uc2  However, a joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  involving the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Europe and Japan after the the weekend meeting is not likely, Solin said. \par \par \uc2  "There's some concern of a highlight of euro weakness.... I don't think it really goes past that," Solin said. \par \par \uc2  Overnight, Germany's Ifo business climate index declined in August for the third consecutive month, raising concern that Europe's largest economy may be slowing and pressuring the euro. \par \par \uc2  "The market is in a situation right now where it's looking...for excuses to sell this thing," and the Ifo survey provided one, Solin said. \par \par \uc2  The December British pound strengthened early after the Bank of England released its latest minutes, which showed the Monetary Policy Committee voted by a slim margin to keep rates on hold. The broker said expectations of a narrowing interest rate differential between Britain and the United States boosted the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Solin said nearby sterling garnered strength from a report that German power giant RWE AG is close to buying Britain's Thames Water Plc for 4.1 billion pounds. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. July trade deficit reached a record $31.89 billion, but the data had little impact on price action. \par \par \uc2  At 9:04 a.m. CDT (1404 GMT), December yen were $0.000027 higher at $0.009523, euros were off $0.00350 at $0.85180, sterling rose $0.0062 to $1.4182, Swiss francs were off $0.0017 at $0.5656, Canadian dollars rose $0.0016 to $0.6760, Australian dollars were $0.0035 lower at $0.5400, and Mexican pesos were down $0.000625 at $0.102825. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw9k076cs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
