\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro propped up by G7 caution, little else. \b0\par\par\uc2 652 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 September 2000\par 05:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sept 19 (Reuters) - The hapless euro enjoyed a rare respite in Tokyo morning trade on Tuesday, as bears played it safe ahead of a weekend meeting of Group of Seven finance ministers. \par \par \uc2  The more cautious tone, which follows the euro's repeated slide to record lows in recent days, came after several European officials sounded off on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fall, although few expect this to translate into concrete help by the G7. \par \par \uc2  "The market is extremely quiet. Sentiment for the euro is still weak, but many players were reluctant to pile up more short positions before the G7 meeting," a Japanese commercial bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "I doubt the euro's trend will be reversed after the G7, but we still have to wait given recent comments by European officials and others." \par \par \uc2  On Monday, Bundesbank President Ernst Welteke said \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  developments would be discussed at the G7 meeting in Prague, adding the euro's moves against the dollar and yen were not justified by fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  Echoing his views, European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  board member Sirkka Hamalainen said she was not happy with the euro's weakness as it did not reflect fundamentals and EU commissioner for Economic Affairs Pedro Solbes also said the euro undervalued by up to 25 percent. \par \par \uc2  At 0210 GMT, the euro stood at $0.8532/37, still within sight of Monday's record low of $0.8510. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen , it was at 91.23/37 yen, not far above its lifetime low around 90.75 yen hit on September 12. \par \par \uc2  Federal Reserve Bank of Dallas President Robert McTeer, however, said on Monday that the euro's weakness may be healthy for Europe's economy if it helps stimulate growth. \par \par \uc2  Such comments strengthen the market view that the ECB will not be able to win support for joint euro-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  The euro tumbled to its latest record low of $0.8510 on Monday after U.S. Federal Reserve Bank of Richmond President Alfred Broaddus said its recent falls raised questions about the long-term viability of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The dollar was steady around 107 yen , but the market lacked direction with many operators sidelined ahead of bookclosings at the end of September. \par \par \uc2  "Basically, many institutions have finished adjusting their positions before the bookclosings, so they don't want to take new positions in dollar/yen," a Japanese trust bank dealer said. "This should make activity in Tokyo thin for a while." \par \par \uc2  Dealers said support was seen around 106.50 yen, while sell orders were lined up slightly above 107.00 yen. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers said the yen was being supported against the dollar by recent fragility in U.S. asset markets, driven by speculation that surging oil prices, which hit a fresh 10-year high overnight, may fuel inflation. \par \par \uc2  At 0239 GMT, the dollar stood at 106.85/95 yen against 106.85/95 yen in U.S. trade late on Monday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0257 GMT. All data taken from Reuters \par \par \uc2  with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130 \par \par \uc2  GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab      Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   1999 Cls\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab   18 Sep.\par \tab \tab \tab      -----------------------------------------\par  Euro/dlr\tab \tab   0.853