\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro sets twin record lows, no respite in sight. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Lisa Jucca \par \uc2 672 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 September 2000\par 09:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Sept 19 (Reuters) - The beleaguered euro hit record lows against the dollar and the yen on Tuesday in the absence of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and was expected to stay pressured as long as central bankers refrained from market action. \par \par \uc2  The hapless single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell as far as $0.8491 EUR=) according to Reuters data, its seventh record low in just 10 sessions. Against the yen, it hit a record low 90.73 EURJPY=). \par \par \uc2  The latest slide came despite a litany of euro-supportive remarks by European officials. Bundesbank President Ernst Welteke said on Monday \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  developments would be discussed at this weekend's Group of Seven industrialised nations meeting in Prague, adding the euro's moves against the dollar and the yen were not justified by economic fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  Along his line, European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  board member Sirkka Hamalainen said she was not happy with the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's softness as it did not reflect fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  But analysts said such talk would not turn the tide, especially against the rampant dollar, which firmed to new record peaks against the Australian and the New Zealand dollar and was near 11-year highs against the Swiss franc. \par \par \uc2  "No one can find a good reason to buy the euro at the moment," said Niels Christensen, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Societe Generale in Paris. \par \par \uc2  "The only thing that could trigger the tide is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , possibly accompanied by soft U.S. data. But with no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in sight for the moment we get what we are seeing at the moment: a weakening euro." \par \par \uc2  By 0730 GMT euro/dollar stood around $0.8520, a third of a cent above its record trough. Euro/yen stood around 91.05. \par \par \uc2  U.S. SEEN AVOIDING \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  Trading in Asia had been initially cautious ahead of the upcoming G7 meeting. \par \par \uc2  Japanese officials, long concerned at the euro's weakness against the yen, tried hard to keep the market wary, with Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa saying Tuesday the euro was sure to be on the agenda at the meeting and Japan's stance was to cooperate to achieve exchange rate stability. \par \par \uc2  But traders said bears were unbowed, arguing that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would only work if the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  joined in and the prospects of that seemed remote at best. \par \par \uc2  "We are comfortable being short the euro because there's no way the U.S. will risk hurting confidence in the dollar when there's an election near and a huge deficit to find," said a European bank dealer in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, Bundesbank President Ernst Welteke conceded that it would be difficult for the Americans to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in an election year. \par \par \uc2  Indeed, Federal Reserve Bank of Dallas President Robert McTeer suggested late on Monday the euro's weakness may be of no concern at all, saying it seemed to be stimulating eurozone economic growth. \par \par \uc2  One potential plus for the euro could be the recent slide in U.S. equities which, was however partly attributable to the euro's weakness eating into corporate earnings there. \par \par \uc2  The tech-laden Nasdaq .IXIC) shed 2.83 percent on Monday while the Dow Jones Industrial .DJI) lost 1.08 percent to hit a six-week low. \par \par \uc2  Longer-dated Treasury prices also extended their sharp losses. Traders were however sceptical the slide was a sign investors were starting to cut their exposure to the U.S as interest rates there still offered an attractive premium over the euro. \par \par \uc2  "You look around the world and you have to ask where else is there to invest than the States?" said the U.S. bank dealer in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  "Take oil prices for instance. Sure they're bad for the U.S. but they're even worse for Europe and Asia. And when funds shift out of Asia there's usually only one safe-haven of choice: America." \par \par \uc2  The dollar was struggling against the yen, trading around 106.80 yen JPY=), the middle of its snug 106.70/107.10 range. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw9j078ll\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
