\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro dips to new life low, more declines seen. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Chikafumi Hodo \par \uc2 996 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 September 2000\par 05:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sept 18 (Reuters) - Speculators attacked the struggling euro again in Tokyo on Monday, sending the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dipping to a new lifetime low as they reckoned chances were faint for joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  After the euro slid to a low of $0.8510, the market was expected to probe key support of $0.8500, where heavy stop-loss and option-linked sell orders are rumoured to be placed, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The euro maintained Friday's downtrend after U.S. Federal Reserve Bank of Richmond President Alfred Broaddus said its recent falls raised questions about the long-term viability of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . However, he said he believed the euro would survive. \par \par \uc2  "A belief that the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) may not be able to ensure support for joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to draw speculative sales," said a European bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  "Sentiment for the euro is extremely weak. The market should be eager to drive it down even further when European participants join the market later in the day." \par \par \uc2  At 0230 GMT, the euro stood at $0.8523/28 against $0.8530/35 in the U.S. late on Friday. Against the yen, it stood at 91.30/44 yen from 91.41 yen on Friday. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday, the euro rallied to above $0.87 after the ECB Bank said it would buy euros with interest income on its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. \par \par \uc2  The market initially took the ECB's decision as a signal the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not allow the European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to fall further, but later shrugged off the move because the ECB's plan to sell 2.5 billion euros of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  over several days was insufficient to reverse its downward trend, traders said. \par \par \uc2  ECB Vice President Christian Noyer said on Sunday the euro was "dangerously undervalued" and its reversal when it comes may be abrupt. \par \par \uc2  In an interview with the French Les Echos daily released ahead of publication on Monday, Noyer said the level of the euro would likely be raised at the G7 meeting of leading industrial nations on Saturday. \par \par \uc2  Although the euro is expected to stay under selling pressure, the market could become wary of selling too aggressively ahead of the Group of Seven meeting, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The euro edged down in thin trade, but, apparently, the market was a bit cautious about overselling," a senior U.S. bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "The market is still sceptical about a joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but for the time being," the dealer said. "People are eager to see the outcome of the G7 meeting." \par \par \uc2  The dollar moved in a tight range against the yen, but held above 107 yen as strong commercial buying and short-covering provided support. \par \par \uc2  Firm dollar buy orders were rumoured placed around 106.80-106.90 yen, while offers by exporters lined up between 107.50-108 yen weighed on the U.S. unit, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "A failure to break above 108 yen last week depressed sentiment for the dollar against the yen," a Japanese trust bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "There is no clear trend in the dollar/yen rate because the movement of the euro is basically setting the overall trend in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," he said. \par \par \uc2  At 0300 GMT, the dollar stood at 107.10/20 yen compared to 107.08/18 yen on Friday. It moved in a range of 107.06 to 107.20 yen in the morning. \par \par \uc2  ECB Vice President Christian Noyer said on Sunday the euro was "dangerously undervalued" and its reversal when it comes may be abrupt. \par \par \uc2  In an interview with the French Les Echos daily released ahead of publication on Monday, Noyer said the level of the euro would likely be raised at the G7 meeting of leading industrial nations on Saturday. \par \par \uc2  Although the euro is expected to stay under selling pressure, the market could become wary of selling too aggressively ahead of the Group of Seven meeting, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The euro edged down in thin trade, but, apparently, the market was a bit cautious about overselling," a senior U.S. bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "The market is still sceptical about a joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but for the time being," the dealer said. "People are eager to see the outcome of the G7 meeting." \par \par \uc2  The dollar moved in a tight range against the yen, but held above 107 yen as strong commercial buying and short-covering provided support. \par \par \uc2  Firm dollar buy orders were rumoured placed around 106.80-106.90 yen, while offers by exporters lined up between 107.50-108 yen weighed on the U.S. unit, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "A failure to break above 108 yen last week depressed sentiment for the dollar against the yen," a Japanese trust bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "There is no clear trend in the dollar/yen rate because the movement of the euro is basically setting the overall trend in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," he said. \par \par \uc2  At 0300 GMT, the dollar stood at 107.10/20 yen compared to 107.08/18 yen on Friday. It moved in a range of 107.06 to 107.20 yen in the morning. \