\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Beleagured euro sees no end to downside in sight. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Deepthi Wickremasinghe \par \uc2 846 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 September 2000\par 14:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Sept 18 (Reuters) - The euro dropped to record lows against the dollar on Monday amid concern that a meeting of the Group of Seven industrial powers this weekend will not result in concerted action to stem the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decline. \par \par \uc2  The euro's latest setback comes after U.S. Federal Reserve Bank of Richmond President Alfred Broaddus said on Friday that the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent falls raised questions about its longer-term survival, although he added he believed the euro would survive. \par \par \uc2  Bundesbank President Ernst Welteke said it would be natural that \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates were discussed at the G7 meeting in Prague at the weekend. \par \par \uc2  Still, Welteke's comments and those of EU Commissioner for Economic Affairs Pedro Solbes and European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Vice President Christian Noyer had little lasting impact on the euro. \par \par \uc2  Talk in the market that the ECB was continuing to buy the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as part of its plan to sell interest income earned on its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, announced last week, gave the euro some support, However, dealers said investors were looking to sell the euro on any rallies. \par \par \uc2  "We have waited so long the market is showing a great ability to be completely disinterested in anything anybody says so the euro probably can't avoid another skid lower," said Kit Juckes, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Royal Bank of Scotland Financial Markets in London. \par \par \uc2  "There is the feeling that we need action." \par \par \uc2  The euro was trading within a quarter cent of record lows just above $0.85 set in Asian trading, having backed off its high for the day around $0.8574. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was orbiting 91, within a half yen of last week's record lows. \par \par \uc2  In addition to his comments on G7, Welteke said that the euro's value against the dollar and the yen was not justified by fundamental factors and that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets was part of the ECB's arsenal. \par \par \uc2  Solbes said the euro was up to 25 percent below its medium-term equilibrium rate. He said better economic policy coordination could help the euro, adding that he saw a risk of higher inflation in Europe but not an inflationary spiral. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, Noyer said in a newspaper interview published on Monday that the euro was "dangerously undervalued" and that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could see a "brutal" rebound. \par \par \uc2  G7 MEETING SEEN OFFERING LITTLE SOLACE \par \par \uc2  Friday's comments from the Richmond Fed's Broaddus about the viability of the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  were seen to have put the market's deep-rooted concern in the spotlight. \par \par \uc2  The comments only added to fears that the euro's 27-percent slide against the dollar from the levels at its birth in 1999 would cause global investors to dump their European bond and stock holdings, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Many analysts suspected that without the help of other G7 partners, notably the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would only have limited impact. But the market remained cautious about expecting too much from the G7 meeting. \par \par \uc2  "No one will take aggressive long euro positions on the basis that G7 might do something," said Steve Barrow, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Bear Stearns in London. \par \par \uc2  "Some European officials have already said it may be difficult for the U.S. to subscribe to too much ahead of the (U.S. presidential) election." \par \par \uc2  He said there was a danger that comments from European officials suggesting the G7 would band together to stem the euro's decline could lead to disappointment in the market if they proved unfounded. \par \par \uc2  "There could be a big let down next week if nothing happens, particularly just a few days ahead of the Danish referendum," Barrow said. \par \par \uc2  The Danes will hold a referendum on joining the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on September 28. \par \par \uc2  The strength of the dollar continued against many \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday despite falls in U.S. stocks on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The Australian dollar fell to record lows against the U.S. unit, with traders blaming its fall on the euro weakness, and the New Zealand dollar dropped towards record lows it had set earlier this month. \par \par \uc2  "One wouldn't have thought the falls in the Dow and the Nasdaq would have been the stuff of dollar strength, but the dollar is strong against a whole raft of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  today," said Juckes at RBS. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar appears to be largely bullet proof. Anyone who has been trying to find cheap levels to buy on the dollar is being bullied out by the price action as opposed to the news." \par \par \uc2  However, dollar strength was making less headway against the yen with the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  supported by gains it had made against the euro. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen had traded as low as 106.71, down around one percent from three-week peaks it had set on Friday around 107.73. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the yen was also buoyed by seasonal factors such as Japanese corporations' profit repatriation ahead of their semi-annual bookclosing at the end of the month. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw9i07cey\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
