\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro under siege, hits record lows vs dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Shinichi Kishima \par \uc2 640 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 September 2000\par 09:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Sept 18 (Reuters) - The euro sank to new record lows against the dollar on Monday amid speculation the Group of Seven industrial powers may not band together to halt the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's slide when they meet this weekend. \par \par \uc2  The euro's latest setback comes after U.S. Federal Reserve Bank of Richmond President Alfred Broaddus said on Friday that its recent falls raised questions about its longer-term survival, although he added he believed the euro would survive. \par \par \uc2  The comments only added to fears that the euro's 27-percent slide against the dollar from the levels at its birth in 1999 would cause global investors to dump their European bond and stock holdings en masse, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Remarks made by European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Vice President Christian Noyer kept traders wary of the risk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but analysts said the pain of holding euro zone European bonds and stocks was becoming excruciating. \par \par \uc2  They said the euro could come under fresh pressure after the euro zone August consumer prices data due out at 1000 GMT, with forecasting for a year-on-year increase of 2.4 percent. \par \par \uc2  "It's building up to pressuring points, and I think the only thing that can stabilise the euro and alleviate these side effects will be coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Neil MacKinnon, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Merrill Lynch in London. \par \par \uc2  "But I think it's only going to be at lower levels." \par \par \uc2  The euro fell to record lows just above $0.85 in Asian trading before clawing its way back up to around $0.8550. Against the yen, the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  managed to stay slightly above last week's record lows below 91. \par \par \uc2  EFFECT OF ECB RESERVES \b \highlight22\uc2 OPERATION\b0 \highlight\uc2  PROVES SHORTLIVED \par \par \uc2  Friday's comments from the Richmond Fed's Broaddus about the viability of the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  were seen to have put the market's deep-rooted concern in the spotlight. \par \par \uc2  "Broaddus touched the most sensitive issue that was in everyone's mind," said Yoshihiko Kobayashi, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  director at HypoVereinsbank AG in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  Kobayashi was sceptical about whether G7 finance ministers meeting in Prague this weekend would be able to engineer a major \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pact to shore up the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Many analysts suspected that without the help of other G7 partners, notably the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would only have limited effect. \par \par \uc2  Such a view was reinforced by the euro's inability to hold on to gains it had made last week in the wake of the ECB's announcement that it would sell 2.5 billion euros worth of interest income on its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. \par \par \uc2  The euro's rebound from the early lows was helped by a newspaper interview published on Monday in which the ECB's Noyer said the euro was "dangerously undervalued" and that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could see a "brutal" rebound. \par \par \uc2  But the market remained cautious about expecting too much from the G7 meeting. \par \par \uc2  "It's really dangerous to expect too much of the G7 outcome. If the outcome is something less than the market expects, then the euro would be sold off again," said Ryohei Muramatsu, manager at Commerzbank in Tokyo. The U.S. Treasury's reluctance to veer away from its "strong dollar" policy, particularly ahead of the November presidential election, was seen to be a major hurdle for policymakers. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was slightly softer against the yen, slipping below the 107 yen JPY=) foothold. \par \par \uc2  The yen was seen buoyed by seasonal factors such as Japanese corporations' profit repatriation ahead of their semi-annual bookclosing at the end of the month. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the Australian dollar fell to record lows against its U.S. counterpart, with traders blaming the euro weakness. The New Zealand dollar also fell toward record lows it had set earlier this month. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw9i07a45\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
