\par\par \b \uc2  Euros collapse, most IMM  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  end lower. \b0\par\par\uc2 521 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2000\par 22:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  CHICAGO, Sept 15 (Reuters) - An unconvincingly brief rally in euro futures sputtered and died on Friday after investors realised a recent move by the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be hardly enough to stall the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's slide, much less prop it higher. \par \par \uc2  Nearly all IMM \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures settled lower on Friday under moderate trading volume. Traders said the euro was to blame for most of the losses in sterling and Swiss franc futures, while yen contracts crept to moderate gains. \par \par \uc2  Japanese markets were closed overnight on Friday for a national holiday, which traders said prompted light volumes in yen futures during U.S. pit trade. \par \par \uc2  December euros bottomed out nearly a full cent lower at $0.85940, a hair above the contract low of $0.85920, and then closed just above the low. \par \par \uc2  One major dealer sold about 6,000 euro spreads minutes ahead of the close, one floor broker said, and "just about crushed them." \par \par \uc2  "There are a lot of people getting out late, waiting until the last day to roll these things," the broker said. \par \par \uc2  The ECB announced on Thursday it would sell the interest income from its foreign reserves for 2.5 billion euros. But prices dropped as the market became wary of the ECB move's effectiveness, and comments later from U.S. Federal Reserve Bank of Richmond President Alfred Broaddus cinched the losses in futures. Broaddus said the recent fall in the euro raised questions about the long-term viability of the euro, although he believed the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would survive. \par \par \uc2  Without joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  and possibly Japan, traders continued to argue that the ECB's chances of reversing the euro's depreciation were slim. \par \par \uc2  "If the euro keeps plummeting, it makes Britain look fantastic," one \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures broker said, "and it's going to be like losing the Second World War. I don't see how (the ECB) can let it slide much further." \par \par \uc2  "The more and more I look at the newspaper, the more and more articles I see" about U.S. companies lowering earnings expectations because of the weak euro, another broker said. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think the U.S. is going to be able to allow this for too much longer." \par \par \uc2  One broker said a commonly held market belief was if the cash euro dropped slightly lower to $0.85150, the ECB would likely move toward direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . This corresponds to about $0.8554 in December euro futures. \par \par \uc2  A busy euro zone calendar over the next two weeks includes the release of Germany's Ifo business sentiment index on Wednesday, next Saturday's meeting of G7 finance ministers, and the Danish vote on inclusion in the euro zone on September 28. \par \par \uc2  December yen settled $0.000024 higher at $0.009468, euros plummeted $0.00910 to $0.85960, Swiss francs were $0.0036 lower at $0.5652, sterling was off $0.0074 at $1.4012, Mexican pesos plunged $0.001450 to $0.103275, Australian dollars were off $0.0042 at $0.5462, and Canadian dollars were up $0.0015 at $0.6753. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw9f07wgv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
