\par\par \b \uc2  Euro on defensive - ECB support still elusive. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Chikafumi Hodo \par \uc2 685 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 September 2000\par 04:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sept 14 (Reuters) - The euro hovered near record lows against the dollar and the yen in Tokyo on Thursday, held down by doubts that a European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governing council meeting later will do little to inspire a recovery. \par \par \uc2  Despite lingering wariness about ECB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , speculators sold euro and were expected to continue unless they saw the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  actually \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen activity was quiet, muffled ahead of end-September bookclosings by Japanese firms and a market holiday in Tokyo on Friday, but exporters were still looking for chances to sell euros heavily against the yen on rallies. \par \par \uc2  "People know that the euro is oversold, but they can't stop," a senior Japanese trust bank trader said. \par \par \uc2  "Looking the way the euro is behaving, the market is ruling out \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but at this point, the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be the effective measure to stop the euro's fall," he said. \par \par \uc2  At 0213 GMT, the euro was quoted at $0.8586/91, compared to Wednesday's late U.S. level of $0.8589/93. The euro hit a record low of $0.8550 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen it was at 92.04/12 yen from Wednesday's 92.04 yen. \par \par \uc2  Few expected the euro to rebound in the absence of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , even if the ECB raises interest rates at Thursday's policy-setting meeting. Dealers said the euro drew little strength from a 25 basis point rate hike two weeks ago. \par \par \uc2  Dealers are focusing on the ECB's news conference at 1230 GMT, after its monetary policy decision announcement at 1145 GMT, for any comments on the euro. \par \par \uc2  In a Reuters poll conducted earlier in the week, all 55 economists surveyed said they expected the ECB to keep its benchmark minimum bidding rate steady at 4.50 percent. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, the euro rose to as high as $0.8703 in overseas markets after the German magazine Focus Money cited French government circles as saying the French presidency of the European Union had begun talks with the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  to get backing for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  A French finance ministry spokeswoman later denied the report. \par \par \uc2  "The market is clearly sensitive to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculation. Looking at the way it had faltered when the report was denied yesterday, not too many operators are serious about seeing the actual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," a European bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "But I feel it is dangerous to rule out the possibility." \par \par \uc2  The dollar stood at 107.18/26 yen from 107.10 yen in late U.S. trading on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was little impact from media reports that the size of direct spending in Japan's extra budget was likely to amount to 3-3.8 trillion yen, since this was within market expectations. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan is widely expected to keep its monetary policy unchanged at a policy board meeting on Thursday and limited market impact was expected in dollar/yen, they said. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, market operators closely focused on the Swiss National Bank's quarterly policy assessment due after 1200 GMT, with the Swiss franc being supported on expectation that SNB would to tighten credit, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was quoted at 1.7683/93 Swiss franc against 1.7719/27 on Wednesday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0223 GMT. All data taken from Reuters \par \par \uc2  with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130 \par \par \uc2  GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab      Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   1999 Cls\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab   13 Sep.\par \tab \tab \tab      -----------------------------------------\par  Euro/dlr\tab \tab   0.8586   0.8593   -0.08   -14.74   1.0070\par  Euro/yen\tab \tab    92.07    91.97   +0.11   -10.70   103.10\par  Dlr/swiss\tab \tab  1.7689   1.7710   -0.12   +11.24   1.5902\par  Stg/dlr\tab \tab    1.4083   1.4092   -0.06   -12.94   1.6176\par  Can/dlr\tab \tab    1.4835   1.4828   +0.05    +2.63   1.4455\par  Aus/dlr\tab \tab    0.5492   0.5540   -0.87   -16.32   0.6563\par  Euro/swiss\tab \tab 1.5189   1.5212   -0.15    -5.28   1.6036\par  Euro/stg\tab \tab   0.6099   0.6091   +0.13    -2.24   0.6239.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw9e084km\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
