\par\par \b \uc2  IMM  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  mixed, euro futures rally dries up. \b0\par\par\uc2 648 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 September 2000\par 16:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  CHICAGO, Sept 13 (Reuters) - Euro futures teetered and fell from early gains on Wednesday and left IMM \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures mixed overall after a brief rally on talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in defence of the struggling euro died out. \par \par \uc2  The December euro contract firmed initially on Wednesday as speculation about possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  filtered through the market. But within an hour and a half of the open, euro futures dropped to just below unchanged and began to chop above and below that level. \par \par \uc2  After Tuesday's gains, December euro futures are not likely to drop below the overnight low of $0.86500, one trader said. \par \par \uc2  "We're seeing a little bit of stabilisation in the euro \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  today," said Frank Lesh, futures analyst at Rand Financial Services. "We've made another leg down in the euro here, and it's hard to get any more short. I guess we're in for a little bit of consolidation now." \par \par \uc2  A report from a German magazine early Wednesday that the French presidency of the European Union was in talks with the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  to secure backing for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the euro was later denied by a French finance ministry spokeswoman. \par \par \uc2  Traders said that while some market participants believed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on some level would be necessary to stabilise the euro, the market as a whole saw no near-term \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in sight. \par \par \uc2  "We've had some talk out of the ECB and there's a possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , although I don't think anybody really believes that," Lesh said. \par \par \uc2  Bundesbank council member Klaus-Dieter Kuehbacher said in a German radio interview overnight that European \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the euro "can only be done together with the Americans." \par \par \uc2  But market participants saw U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as an unlikely prospect. \par \par \uc2  "I think the U.S. is very reluctant to be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Lesh said. "Our Treasury just doesn't feel that that's a real effective way to get things done." \par \par \uc2  The market awaited a news conference scheduled for the tail end of an ECB policymaking meeting on Thursday for possible comments on the euro from ECB officials. Investors also speculated, traders said, that a Group of Seven meeting on Sept. 23 could result in a common statement of support for the euro. \par \par \uc2  December yen posted a three-week low of $0.009465 early on Wednesday after crashing down into the gap posted between Aug. 22 and 23 from $0.009503 to $0.009430. \par \par \uc2  But yen futures bounced into more more shallow negative territory after a set of U.S. economic data showed import prices rose in August while export prices posted the largest drop since March of last year. \par \par \uc2  December yen seem "destined" to head toward a shelf of support levels scattered within a band of congestion at the late July to mid-August ranges, Lesh said. In the event of a downmove, the contract is likely to stall near $0.009440 or just lower near $0.009412. \par \par \uc2  One floor broker said the market's orientation was centred on U.S. producer price index data slated for release on Thursday and consumer price index data scheduled for Friday. \par \par \uc2  "That's the real story," Lesh said of the upcoming data. "It's the dollar against the world right now." \par \par \uc2  Economists polled by Reuters expected both the core PPI and CPI figures and their ex-food and energy components to increase by 0.2 percent. \par \par \uc2  At 9:14 a.m. CDT (1414 GMT), December yen were $0.000031 lower at $0.009479, euros wer up $0.00010 at $0.86690, sterling rose $0.0028 to $1.4116, Swiss francs were up $0.0011 at $0.5717, Canadian dollars dropped $0.0013 to $0.6753, Australian dollars were $0.0028 lower at $0.5562, and Mexican pesos were off $0.000625 at $0.104600. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw9d081ej\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
