\par\par \b \uc2  Buba's Kuehbacher-can't prop euro without U.S. help. \b0\par\par\uc2 198 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 September 2000\par 10:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  FRANKFURT Sept 13 (Reuters) - Bundesbank council member Klaus-Dieter Kuehbacher said on Wednesday that \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the ailing euro would make sense only if the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped. \par \par \uc2  "A unilateral \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the European side is not at all possible," Kuehbacher said in an interview on Germany's Deutschlandfunk radio. \par \par \uc2  "It (\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) can only be done together with the Americans," Kuehbacher added. \par \par \uc2  The International Monetary Fund and Group of Seven meetings in Prague next week could provide the opportunity to speak about possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Kuehbacher added. \par \par \uc2  Kuehbacher said there were two sides of the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  coin: those who were holding dollars must be willing to sell them on the market, while those who want a stronger euro must be willing to buy euros. \par \par \uc2  It makes no sense that on the one hand, the U.S. is interested in a strong dollar and on the other hand, the Europeans are interested in a strong euro, he said. \par \par \uc2  Kuehbacher sits on the Bundesbank's council but has no vote on the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's council, which sets monetary policy for the euro zone. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw9d081a9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
