\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-Joint  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  on euro in US interest-Prodi. \b0\par\par\uc2 452 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 September 2000\par 11:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BERLIN, Sept 12 (Reuters) - European Commission President Romano Prodi said on Tuesday it was in the interests of the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  with other central banks to support the euro. \par \par \uc2  Prodi, in interview extracts to be published by Germany's Stern magazine on Thursday, said joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be in the interests of Washington because the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  balance of payments deficit was too high. \par \par \uc2  Asked if joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by central banks in Europe, the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Japan would help, Prodi was quoted as saying: "...we have now reached the point where it would be in the American interest." He conceded such a move would be unlikly ahead of the U.S.-presidential election. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's record-breaking rally on foreign exchanges has made it tougher for U.S. exporters to compete on world markets, while making imports cheaper. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. current account deficit is running at around four percent of gross domestic product - a level clearly regarded by Prodi as unsustainable. \par \par \uc2  "Nobody can live with such a balance of payments deficit forever," Prodi told Stern, which released a one-page interview summary ahead of publication. \par \par \uc2  Prodi's remarks were published after the euro set new record lows against the greenback of $0.8553, down 27 percent from its January 1999 launch. The common European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has fallen by around a third against the Japanese yen. \par \par \uc2  He conceded, however, that it would be hard to organise joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  before the U.S. presidential elections in November. \par \par \uc2  Prodi said the euro's exchange rate was "disappointingly" low and said one reason behind the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's weakness was the lack of a common European economic policy. \par \par \uc2  "That has definitely had an influence on the euro exchange rate," Prodi, Italy's former prime minister, said. \par \par \uc2  He added that he was happy that the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  enjoyed independent status. "But it lacks a political partner with which it can hold a dialogue." \par \par \uc2  Prodi said the euro would win more confidence on financial markets if there were a common European government, but added he was not calling for the creation of a federal European state. \par \par \uc2  The EU commission chief's comments came after the so-called Euro Group of countries said last Friday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not reflect the bloc's strong economic fundamentals but failed in a joint statement to address the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue. \par \par \uc2  The Euro Group, comprising the euro zone's 11 member states and Greece, which joins next year, was set up as an informal forum before the euro's launch and is regarded as a potential joint economic government, but currently has no formal decision making powers. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw9c08evx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
