\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-Japan spent Y1.4 trln in Apr to boost dlr. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Masayuki Kitano \par \uc2 475 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 August 2000\par 04:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Aug 7 (Reuters) - Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) published for the first time on Monday the amount of its foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , saying it spent 1.3854 trillion yen ($12.78 billion) in the April-June quarter to buy dollars. The sum was used in a single \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on April 3, it said. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan, which acts as the MOF's agent in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has intermittently stepped into the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since last year to prevent a rapid appreciation of the yen against the dollar that Japanese authorities fear may choke of the tentative economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  The yen has been appreciating since last year on hopes for a recovery in Japan and on concerns of an economic slowdown in the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  A MOF official told reporters the decision to publicise \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  amounts, which the ministry had kept a closely guarded secret, was made to bring Japan's disclosure practices in line with international standards. \par \par \uc2  Currently, the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  publicises the amount of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  every quarter, and Britain has announced its intention to begin publicising such data in the future. The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not made clear what it wants to do. The official said the ministry would from now on publicise the total \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  amount for each quarter, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  used for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the date of each \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  All foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducted using Japan's special \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account, including \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that foreign central banks conduct on Japan's behalf, will be contained in the figures, the MOF official said. \par \par \uc2  "There are various ways to conduct \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and all \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for our special \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account will be included," the official said. \par \par \uc2  "For example, if we ask the U.S. FRB (Federal Reserve Board) to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on our behalf, that will be included in the data," he said. \par \par \uc2  The ministry, however, was cautious as to whether the new disclosure standards will be implemented retroactively for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducted before April. "We would like to study our response to this matter taking into account whether such a move would cause market players to speculate on our future actions in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets," he said. \par \par \uc2  The ministry said Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves swelled to a record $344.89 billion at the end of July, eclipsing the previous record of $344.85 billion set in June. \par \par \uc2  The reserves - securities and deposits denominated in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , International Monetary Fund (IMF) reserve positions, IMF special drawing rights (SDRs) and gold - have now risen for eight successive months. It maintained its policy of not giving a reason for the change in the reserves. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 5473 3748 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dw8700t8s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
