\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 2-Japan MOF spent Y1.4 trln to boost dollar in April. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Masayuki Kitano \par \uc2 624 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 August 2000\par 08:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Aug 7 (Reuters) - Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) surprised the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Monday when it revealed details of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time saying it sold 1.385 trillion yen ($12.88 billion) for dollars in the April-June quarter. \par \par \uc2  All the yen-selling came on April 3 said the MOF, whose unveiling of the figures increases public accountability. Such \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is funded by government borrowing which may lead to an increased burden on taxpayers. \par \par \uc2  Analysts welcomed the move but some said the MOF could go further by revealing more in-depth data and market analysis. \par \par \uc2  "This is a good development and will enable the public to check the MOF's actions and gauge the effectiveness of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Taisuke Tanaka, strategist for Credit Suisse First Boston's Tokyo branch. \par \par \uc2  The yen has been appreciating since last year on hopes for an economic recovery in Japan and concern of a slowdown in the economy of the United States. \par \par \uc2  Prospects for a nation's economic expansion can fuel speculation of an increase in demand for its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  prompted by likely extra spending by firms and individuals, pushing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  higher. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan - the MOF's agent in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealings - has intermittently stepped into the market in the past year to prevent further rises in the yen which Japanese authorities fear may choke the nation's tentative economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  A MOF official told reporters that publication of the data would bring Japan in line with international standards. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  publicises the amount of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  every quarter and Britain has announced its intention to begin revealing such data. The ministry will reveal the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  amount, \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  involved and transaction dates, including deals conducted by foreign central banks on its behalf, said the MOF official. \par \par \uc2  "For example, if we ask the U.S. FRB (Federal Reserve Board) to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on our behalf, that will be included," he said. \par \par \uc2  PUBLIC PERUSAL \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  amount was close to market estimates for dollar-buying of $13.2 billion in April, but analysts said such estimates have not always been reliable and praised the MOF for raising transparency. \par \par \uc2  "It is a huge step forward," said Sayuri Kawamura, senior economist for Japan Research Institute. "The new standards will...enable the public to check whether the MOF has increased government borrowing for the purpose of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in vain," Kawamura said. \par \par \uc2  The MOF funds yen-selling by issuing short-term government bonds, known as financing bills, which are also sold to fill in short-term gaps in public coffers. \par \par \uc2  Such public accountability is becoming more crucial at a time when Japan's total government debt is forecast to rise to a record 645 trillion yen by next March. \par \par \uc2  But Kawamura said the MOF should go further and emulate the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  by saying why it decided to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and explain the assessment of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market trends which prompted the action. \par \par \uc2  Another way disclosure could be improved would be to reveal details of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and levels of external reserves - gold and foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  denominated assets held by the government - prior to April, based on the new standards, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "But the MOF may be reluctant to do so since such disclosure could bring the policies of former top MOF officials...back under public scrutiny," said CSFB's Tanaka. \par \par \uc2  MOF officials were indeed cautious about such a move. \par \par \uc2  "We would like to...take into account whether such a move would cause market players to speculate on our future actions in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets," he said. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 5473 3748 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dw8700d04\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
