\par\par \b \uc2  ANALYSIS-Euro rebound provides narrow window for ECB action. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Shinichi Kishima \par \uc2 700 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Mai 2000\par 15:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, May 30 (Reuters) - The euro's latest rebound is presenting the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  with a rare opportunity for successful \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to mark a definitive end to the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's protracted decline, analysts said on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  A combination of a U.S. stock market selloff, improving euro zone economic outlook, a favourable technical picture and verbal support has pushed the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  up more than six percent against the dollar from record lows hit earlier in the month. \par \par \uc2  The ECB has repeatedly expressed its concerns about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  against market trends and without support from other major central banks. But a raft of aggressive comments from European officials over the past two days have raised hopes that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a possibility. \par \par \uc2  Analysts think that current conditions could allow a narrow open window for such an action. \par \par \uc2  "Given the better mood, right now would be a fantastic time to back up their rhetoric with action," said Jim O'Neill, chief economist at Goldman Sachs in London, adding that without such a strong action the latest rebound could be another false dawn. \par \par \uc2  "Fortunately, because of what happened to the U.S. equity market last week and the week before, the rhetoric is having an impact. But if the U.S. equity market recovers, it will lose its importance," he said. \par \par \uc2  The euro rose to five-week highs above $0.94 on Monday, up more than six percent from the record lows around $0.8845 hit on May 4 and retested on May 17. \par \par \uc2  Technical analysts noted that the euro rallied on Friday past $0.92, the interim peak in between these two major troughs, to confirm a so-called "double bottom" basing formation - with the verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the background adding fuel. \par \par \uc2  FAVOURABLE CONDITION FOR \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  The rally removes a key obstacle to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , since historically this tends to succeed when reinforcing a market trend. \par \par \uc2  The most celebrated coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the floating exchange rate era followed the Plaza Accord of September 1985 when the world's rich nations worked together to weaken the dollar, only beginning coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the dollar had began to soften. \par \par \uc2  "Now that the euro is moving in the right direction, it's a favourable condition for them to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , rather than trying to stop it on the way down," said Claudio Piron, treasury economist at Standard Chartered Bank in London. \par \par \uc2  "But I still think there are divisions among them about what to do, so they're certainly talking it up as much as they can. \par \par \uc2  However, another obstacle to successful \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been the lack of interest by the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  in propping up the euro, and there is no sign the authorities there have changed their minds. \par \par \uc2  The euro's recovery began picking up steam last week as policymakers stepped up their rhetoric and gave the market the impression that they were getting more serious about shoring up the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, French Prime Minister Lionel Jospin urged the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and euro zone countries to join forces in analysing the euro's woes and consider joint action in response. \par \par \uc2  The remarks followed Bundesbank President Ernst Welteke's comment on Monday that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was part of "central bankers' toolkit" and a raft of other recent euro-jawboning. \par \par \uc2  French President Jacques Chirac also on Monday suggested that the euro zone exploit good economic times to pursue structural reforms, addressing the market's longer-term concerns. \par \par \uc2  Steve Barrow, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Bear Stearns in London, said the euro recovery could easily fizzle out, perhaps in the $0.96-0.97 area. \par \par \uc2  "Up there, when the market starts to ask itself questions about where we go from there, the answer is inevitably down again because nothing fundamental has changed." \par \par \uc2  "In history, in periods where \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have got excessive undervaluation or overvaluation, markets have have had an incapability to correct themselves naturally. Very often they have to be guided by central banks - and the guidance generally has to be a lot more than just jawboning." ((London Capital Markets +44-20-7542-6721, shinichi.kishima@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw5u04gx1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
