\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar inches up vs euro ahead of FOMC. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Shinichi Kishima \par \uc2 573 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Mai 2000\par 14:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, May 16 (Reuters) - The dollar inched up against the euro on Tuesday amid fading prospects of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , although trading was slow ahead of a U.S. Federal Reserve policy meeting. \par \par \uc2  While the Federal Open Market Committee was widely expected to raise U.S. interest rates by a half percentage point, traders said the market was holding its breath to see what the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had to say on its future policy. \par \par \uc2  So far, they said, they saw little to undermine the market's confidence that the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would engineer a soft landing for the booming U.S. economy. \par \par \uc2  "A lot of it has been priced in already," said Michael Lewis, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at Deutsche Bank in London. "Even with a 50 basis point rise, I don't think that's going to curb people's optimism on the U.S. economy." \par \par \uc2  The Fed will announce its interest rate decision at 1815 GMT. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was drifting in the upper end of a tight range against the euro EUR=), consolidating about a cent off last Friday's two-week troughs around $0.92. \par \par \uc2  According to a Reuters poll conducted on Friday, 27 of 29 primary dealers expected a half-point increase in the Fed's target for the federal funds rate to 6.50 percent. \par \par \uc2  "If we get a 50 basis point rate hike, it would be no shakes and I don't think there would be a huge fall-out in the dollar or U.S. assets, unless there is a frightening statement accompanying it," said Cameron Crise, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Warburg Dillon Read in London. \par \par \uc2  EURO \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  FEARS WANE \par \par \uc2  Traders said the euro had lost some of its recent lustre as wariness of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  waned. \par \par \uc2  Short-covering on fears of such \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action had been cited as the main reason for the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recovery from record lows below $0.89 set early this month. But traders said there was a limit to how long the euro could garner support from such a factor in the absence of actual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "I think expectation of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that has supported the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will diminish in time and you'll see a renewed bout of euro weakness going forward," said Ryan Shea, international economist at Bank One in London. \par \par \uc2  The euro briefly dipped after Bundesbank President Ernst Welteke was quoted by German business daily Handelsblatt as saying he did not expect the big \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  blocs - Europe, the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Japan - to stage concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the coming months. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think the comments were very wise or helpful and I don't know whether they were sanctioned by other members of the ECB," said Marian Bell, treasury economist at Royal Bank of Scotland. \par \par \uc2  "To rule out \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at this stage is not very helpful, given it is one of the things the ECB could do if the euro started falling again." \par \par \uc2  Against the yen JPY=), the dollar hove