\par\par \b \uc2  Welteke sees no concerted  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  in next mths. \b0\par\par\uc2 208 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Mai 2000\par 08:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  FRANKFURT, May 16 (Reuters) - Bundesbank President Ernst Welteke was reported on Tuesday as saying he did not expect the big \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  blocs Europe, the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Japan to stage concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the euro in coming months. \par \par \uc2  Welteke was reported in German business daily Handelsblatt as saying he was opposed to unilateral \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and that the U.S. were unlikely to want to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the euro before the presidential election in the autumn. \par \par \uc2  Welteke is a member of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Governing Council. \par \par \uc2  "Concerted means everyone must have an interest in it (\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 )," Welteke was quoted as saying. He also said the weak level of the euro was unjustifiable. "The trend turnaround must now come at some time," Welteke said, according to Handelsblatt. \par \par \uc2  Welteke also said an eventual increase in U.S. interest rates by a full point, as urged by the Organisation for Economic Co-\b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Development last week, would "mean a further capital inflow into the U.S. with effects on the euro." \par \par \uc2  Then the ECB would have to ask itself the question "whether we have to increase interest rates as well," Welteke said. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw5g00h98\par }\page {\par\fs