\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro extends gains, all eyes on ECB. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Shinichi Kishima \par \uc2 602 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Mai 2000\par 12:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, May 10 (Reuters) - The euro rose to one-week highs against the dollar and the yen on Wednesday amid lingering wariness of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its support and speculation of higher euro zone interest rates. \par \par \uc2  While the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had yet to take any direct action on the beleagured single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a growing perception that authorities' patience was wearing thin tipped the risk/reward scale in favour of buying the euro, traders said. \par \par \uc2  In addition, talk the ECB was considering a change in its money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  that could lead to higher euro zone interest rates also helped the euro move further away from last week's record lows. \par \par \uc2  "If you don't have any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  or rate hikes, it is possible that the market would be disappointed," said Francesca Fornasari, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at Lehman Brothers in London. \par \par \uc2  "But people are beginning to think that at these levels, the threat that something might happen should the euro get weaker is certainly there." The euro rose to one-week highs above $0.91 and 99.50 yen in Europe, extending its recovery from last week's life lows around $0.8850 and 95.60 yen. \par \par \uc2  The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also rose to two-week highs just short of 60 pence against sterling, which was undermined by speculation that UK interest rates might be nearing a peak. \par \par \uc2  The pound fell to four-year lows against the dollar below $1.5240 after the Bank of England's quarterly inflation report forecast tame inflation and slower economic growth. \par \par \uc2  ECB POLICY IN FOCUS \par \par \uc2  Analysts said comments by European officials in recent days had fuelled talk the ECB could be ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time to support the euro, although they said the timing might not necessarily be quite right yet. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a possibility, but the timing is really crucial," said Fabio Fraschetti, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Banca Nazionale del Lavoro in London. \par \par \uc2  The frisson of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fear had been amplified by rumours in New York the Financial Times newspaper would carry a report claiming the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  was ready, if asked, to join concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But dealers said the actual article, entitled "Is Europe misinterpreting signals from Washington", was not nearly as strong as speculation had suggested. \par \par \uc2  Still, with only a day before the ECB'S fortnightly policy meeting on Thursday, the euro received a further boost from a report in a German newspaper that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was weighing a change in its market \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The daily Boersen Zeitung said the ECB was "intensively considering" a switch to a variable rate liquidity tender from its present fixed-rate regime, a move which would give the market more sway in determining interest rates and likely leading to higher rates. \par \par \uc2  The dollar remained buoyant against the dollar, holding just below Tuesday's two-month highs around 109.60 yen. \par \par \uc2  The yen was broadly undermined by a decline in the Tokyo stock market's Nikkei average and by widening yield differentials between U.S. and Japanese bonds. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also under pressure from speculative sales triggered by Tuesday's announcement that Japanese mobile phone firm NTT Docomo would purchase a 15 percent stake in Dutch firm KPN Mobile for five billion euros. \par \par \uc2  "It's got people wondering if this is the start of a trend: a new wave of Japanese investment offshore, which would go some way to recycling Japan's current account surplus and lessening the upward pressure on the yen," said the U.S. bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw5a00vf5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
