\par\par \b \uc2  ANALYSIS-ECB reserves in focus as Ecofin meets. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Shinichi Kishima \par \uc2 764 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Mai 2000\par 15:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, May 5 (Reuters) - Pressure is mounting on European authorities to change tack on their policy toward the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's huge \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves as the euro's decline accelerated to historic lows this week. \par \par \uc2  With the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  losing nearly a quarter of its value against the dollar since its launch in January 1999, market analysts said it was time European Union finance ministers recognised the failure of trying to convince the market with the sheer size of the ECB's yet untapped war chest. \par \par \uc2  EU finance ministers meet on Monday in Brussels at a regular Ecofin meeting where the plight of the euro is expected to overshadow the rest of the agenda. \par \par \uc2  Jim O'Neill, chief economist at Goldman Sachs in London, said the ECB and the national central banks (NCBs) of the euro member countries have too large a stockpile of reserves, and now is the time to liquidate them and buy the euro. \par \par \uc2  He said the spectre of sustained euro buying to liquidate tens of billions of dollars in excess ECB reserves could have more impact on the market than ordinary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , let alone just warnings of such an action. \par \par \uc2  "I suspect what they will end up doing is just agreeing on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but I think it would be more powerful for the Ecofin to send is a statement on excess reserves," O'Neill said. \par \par \uc2  The amount of imports into euro zone is significantly smaller than aggregate imports into individual countries before the introduction of the European Economic and Monetary Union in 1999, thereby reducing the required reserves levels, he noted. \par \par \uc2  ECOFIN TO DISCUSS RAISING RESERVE LIMIT \par \par \uc2  Ironically, Monday's meeting had been slated to rule on the ECB's request to effectively double the limit of its discretionary reserves. \par \par \uc2  The ECB asked in September 1999 for enabling powers to effectively double its reserves, if needed, to 100 billion euros. \par \par \uc2  European officials have said, however, ministers on Monday would only allow for further call-ups needed to "replenish" holdings up to the 50 billion euro reserves limit in the Bank's statute. \par \par \uc2  But increasing the capacity means little, given the NCBs already have a further 150 billion euros or so of their own reserves in addition to the ECB's already huge reserves. \par \par \uc2  "The reserves were initially set at a very high level in order to reinforce confidence in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and clearly that has been a failure," said Nick Parsons, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Commerzbank in London. \par \par \uc2  "Confidence in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not been sustained by having a high level of reserves - the only way to restore confidence is to use the reserves. That's what they're there for." \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro fell as low as $0.8844\tab   on Thursday, down nearly 25 percent from its $1.1747 debut in January 1999, accelerating its slide in recent weeks despite evidence of a pickup in the euro zone economy and big pullbacks in the U.S. stock market, which still remains highly volatile.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Traders said a lack of concrete Ecofin action could be disastrous, particularly as the market has pushed the euro back up slightly toward the psychological $0.90 level on Friday, paying some respect to their firepower.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "People with short positions have squared up, and some people may have even gone long euros, so you could see a lot of fresh selling and loss-cutting next week if we see nothing from the authorities," said Junpei Yamamoto, head of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at the Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Traders said the market's wariness of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  action was heightened on Friday after ECB President Wim Duisenberg's unprecedented ad-hoc statement that the ECB would "do all it can" to keep prices stable.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Duisenberg also said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was aware of euro area citizens' concerns about the value of their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and was monitoring the exchange rate "very closely".\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The ECB is said to be reluctant to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on the market unless the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 United States\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , if not the entire Group of Seven industrial powers, acted in concert.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But analysts say the ECB must first show its own resolve about restoring stability in its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Given the potential nasty consequences of continued euro weakness for the rest of the world, the G7 would immediately follow them, but they need to take the lead," O'Neill at Goldman said. "The market is sick of words, we need action." ((London Capital Markets +44-20-7542-6721, shinichi.kishima@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 2000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw5501ax9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
