\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro crumbles to record low vs dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Carolyn Cohn \par \uc2 723 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Januar 2000\par 12:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Jan 28 (Reuters) - The euro fell to record lows against the dollar on Friday with the absence of any official support for the ailing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fuelling a two-cent slide below parity in as many days. \par \par \uc2  Concern about the relative growth and political outlook in the euro zone in comparison with the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2 , coupled with lack of verbal or direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , sent the euro     to a low of $0.9830, its third record low this week. \par \par \uc2  This was more than 16 percent below the level at which it was launched with champagne celebrations in January 1999, and equivalent to the once-mighty German mark's lowest levels against the dollar in more than 10 years. \par \par \uc2  "It's the usual culprits at work," said Glenn Davies, chief economist at Credit Lyonnais in London. "It's the strength of the U.S. economy, and politics in Europe." \par \par \uc2  Analysts said in addition to economic concerns, the euro was suffering from a range of political issues undermining the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's credibility. \par \par \uc2  These included lack of structural reform in euro-zone economies, the financial scandal surrounding former German chancellor and euro architect Helmut Kohl which has threatened to embroil France, and the possibility of the far-right Freedom Party joining the Austrian government. \par \par \uc2  Traders said there was no sign the euro's downward momentum was waning and that the euro could be headed toward $0.9779, equivalent to 2.00 marks in dollar/mark terms, and below there to $0.95. \par \par \uc2  "The euro is really suffering and this is now a fresh phase of weakness," said Brian Kiely, strategist at Royal Bank of Scotland in London. \par \par \uc2  The euro was trading around $0.9855 at 1030 GMT. \par \par \uc2  LACKLUSTRE OFFICIALS \par \par \uc2  Traders said the euro's decline accelerated this week after finance ministers of the Group of Seven industrial powers made no mention of its weakness in a communique issued after a meeting in Japan last Saturday. \par \par \uc2  They said European officials' remarks also appeared lacklustre in the face of the falls, despite numerous opportunities for officials to speak on the sidelines of the World Economic Forum in Davos, Switzerland. \par \par \uc2  Bundesbank President Ernst Welteke said in Davos the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not neglect exchange rate developments, as they were a key element of the bank's two-pillar strategy. \par \par \uc2  "The bottom line is, what are they going to do about it?" said a dealer at a Japanese bank in London, adding that the infant European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had yet to instil the kind of fear in the market that the U.S. Federal Reserve and other central banks have over the years with aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Traders said fear of such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the euro's behalf was watered down after ECB Chief Economist Otmar Issing said earlier this week there were no euro exchange levels at which it would be automatically triggered. \par \par \uc2  A stabilisation in the U.S. stock market, which was seen to have discounted a Fed rate hike at next week's Federal Open Market Committee meeting, also made the euro less attractive, they added. \par \par \uc2  However, if the fourth quarter U.S. gross domestic product and employment cost index due out at 1330 GMT showed signs of overheating in the U.S. economy and hit Wall Street stocks, the euro could find some short-term relief, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The euro failed to find support from French unemployment data showing a drop in the jobless rate to 10.6 percent in December, or from an acceleration in euro-zone M3 money supply growth to a 12-month rate of 6.4 percent, from 6.2 percent in November. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro also came within a whisker of Thursday's 60.22-pence record low against the British pound\tab      and barely a yen above 102-yen record lows it set against the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab      in early January.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro also dragged the Swiss franc lower in its wake, pushing the franc to 10-year lows near 1.64 to the dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar was softer against the yen\tab  , pressured by the weakness in euro/yen to one-week lows below 105 yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((London Capital Markets +44 171 542 6320, carolyn.cohn@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 2000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw1s07olb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
