\par\par \b \uc2  Japan MOF Mizoguchi won't discuss  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 168 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Oktober 1999\par 03:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Oct 28 (Reuters) - Senior Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) official Zembei Mizoguchi said on Thursday the ministry would consider an appropriate response to the yen's rise but declined to discuss the possibility of market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Asked about the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , either by Japan alone or with the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2 , after the yen pushed to a one-month high of 103.72 to the dollar overnight, Mizoguchi told reporters he could not discuss anything specific about \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "We are always cooperating, in contact with, various countries as needed," he said. "As was said in the G7 (Group of Seven industrial nations) statement, we will monitor the market and cooperate." \par \par \uc2  Mizoguchi said there was no change in MOF's stance that a rapid yen rise was unfavourable and that the ministry will closely watch market conditions and consider an appropriate response. ((William Mallard, Tokyo newsroom +81-3 3432-8022 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010909dvas017t0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
